  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Academy for Women Entrepreneurs (AWE) - - MAKUR PEANUT BUTTER</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sector: Women&apos;s Entrepreneurship.Beneficiaries: 153 women.Description: Grantee is providing training to 153 small holder women farmers in production of quality peanuts using improved seed varieties and reduce aflatoxin contamination. To meet growing demand for peanut butter in schools the company seeks a packing machine to increase efficiency in packing their product. By providing training to small holder farmers in production of quality peanuts the company is able to offer healthy and finely processed affordable, portable, and durable peanut butter to customers and raise farmer incomes.</narrative>
  </description>
